WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:01.089
People: Good morning, Hank!

00:00:01.089 --> 00:00:02.089
It's Friday.

00:00:02.089 --> 00:00:06.300
John: Hank you just got said 'hello' to by
Josh Lewis, Holly Black, Cassie Clare and

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.000
the great Maureen Johnson.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.710
As you can tell from the gray speckled walls
behind me, I am currently in an airport.

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:14.900
Actually, you're probably watching this in
the future, in which case I'm hopefully not

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:16.030
currently in an airport.

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:20.130
Unless you're one of these people, in which
case you're watching me in the present and

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.130
I am currently in an airport.

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:24.910
So I've been in New York for the last couple
days meeting with my publisher, Julie Strauss-Gabel,

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:29.440
and my agent, Jodi Reamer, to talk about The
Fault in Our Stars and all the wonderful things

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:31.710
that are happening, none of which I can tell
you about.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:35.300
Do you know what I do, by the way, when I'm
in airports and my flight is delayed and I

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.800
have an hour to kill?

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:39.280
I sign The Fault in Our Stars!

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:43.130
I brought two thousand sheets to sign today.

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:44.969
It's a green pen day, in case you're wondering.

00:00:44.969 --> 00:00:47.510
I get excited about, like, what the color
day is.

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:50.560
I wake up and one of the first thoughts I
have is, 'Is it a purple day?

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:51.969
I hope it's a purple day.'

00:00:51.969 --> 00:00:52.969
But it's not.

00:00:52.969 --> 00:00:53.980
It's always a green day.

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:58.360
Oh that would be a good name for a band...
Green Day...

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:01.140
So Hank because I spend about six hours a
day signing my name over and over again, I've

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:04.750
been thinking a lot about my signature and
its many inefficiencies.

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:08.081
I mean there's the obvious problem of the
complete illegibility of my signature, but

00:01:08.081 --> 00:01:11.119
another disappointment about it is that it's
totally inconsistent.

00:01:11.119 --> 00:01:14.740
Like sometimes it looks relatively good, like
this one, and then sometimes there are ones

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:17.939
like this one that are just you know, tragically
and irrevocably flawed.

00:01:17.939 --> 00:01:21.439
And the weirdest part is that when I try to
explain to Sarah about these tragic and irrevocable

00:01:21.439 --> 00:01:24.340
flaws in some of my signatures, she thinks
that I'm crazy.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:27.689
She says that's the exact same signature as
any other signature, but let me tell you,

00:01:27.689 --> 00:01:31.609
when you spend six hours a day looking at
your signature over and over and over again

00:01:31.609 --> 00:01:35.560
in fifty-seven thousand iterations, you start
to notice the little things.

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:38.409
You know, like the amount of volume in the
J-Scribble and whether the hooble-dee-hoo

00:01:38.409 --> 00:01:41.460
lines up with the whattidy-what in the J.
Which is not even to mention the variable

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:43.509
length of the gooble-de-gook over here at
the end end of my signature.

00:01:43.509 --> 00:01:46.499
Also, this whosidy-what up here, sometimes
I don't even write that because my hand goes

00:01:46.499 --> 00:01:47.499
off the paper.

00:01:47.499 --> 00:01:48.499
It's a disaster!

00:01:48.499 --> 00:01:51.079
Hank, I just had one of those "The people
at the airport think that I'm crazy" moments,

00:01:51.079 --> 00:01:55.340
and it occurred to me that, uh, you probably
also think that I'm crazy.

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:58.739
I hope that I'm not suffering from Signing
Madness.

00:01:58.739 --> 00:01:59.739
That's a disease, you know.

00:01:59.739 --> 00:02:00.859
I made it up, but it's a disease.

00:02:00.859 --> 00:02:03.170
Hank, let's go see if there's anything interesting
in the airport.

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:05.399
Look at all the free iPads, that's interesting.

00:02:05.399 --> 00:02:06.399
Pizza is interesting.

00:02:06.399 --> 00:02:09.000
A monument to dead sheep is kinda interesting.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.000
Right, so funny story.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.849
By the way, John from the future here, I'm
in a different airport, but anyway.

00:02:12.849 --> 00:02:15.980
Right after I said that thing about how it's
sort of interesting to see a monument to a

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:18.909
dead sheep, a police office walked up to me
and said, "What are you doing?"

00:02:18.909 --> 00:02:21.739
And I said, "I'm filming a monument to a deceased
sheep."

00:02:21.739 --> 00:02:23.110
And he said, "Why are ya doin' that?"

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:27.659
and I said, "It's a really, really long story."

00:02:27.659 --> 00:02:31.590
And then he just looked at me for a while,
and finally I said, "Is it illegal?" and he

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:33.049
said, "I don't know!"

00:02:33.049 --> 00:02:36.750
And so I was like, "Well as long as we're
in this legal gray area, can I keep doing

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:37.750
it?"

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:38.750
and he said, "You probably shouldn't."

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:39.750
So thus ends the vlog.

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:43.099
I have to go get on a different airplane because
the previous airplane wasn't fun enough.

00:02:43.099 --> 00:02:45.129
But Hank, I will see you on Friday!

00:02:45.129 --> 00:02:48.400
Unless it is Friday, in which case I will
see you on Monday!

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.040
Sorry, I don't have my calendar with me!

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:54.020
Hi, it's John from the future future, I made
it back home, so that's good.

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:57.909
Quick P.S., in the great tradition of older
brothers, I have taken a cool toy that my

00:02:57.909 --> 00:03:00.490
little brother enjoyed playing with and stolen
it.

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:02.230
I am referring, of course, to the YouTube
channel hankgames.

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:06.400
I have started a series of video's in which
I play FIFA while telling you stories of my

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:07.400
life.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:10.469
So, for instance, if you click on my face
right now, you will be taken to a video where

00:03:10.469 --> 00:03:15.590
I am playing as the Swindon Town Swoodilypoopers
while simultaneously telling you about how

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:17.049
I met and courted the Yeti.

00:03:17.049 --> 00:03:19.969
So you can check that out there and if you
like it, subscribe, and thank- Hey!

00:03:19.969 --> 00:03:22.319
Look, it's my calendar!

00:03:22.319 --> 00:03:23.620
I missed you, calendar!

